  "faqs": [
    { "q": "Why put a system on a service contract?", "a": "Water treatment equipment works quietly in the background, which is exactly why problems can go unnoticed until performance drops or a failure interrupts supply. A service contract means the system is checked, sampled and adjusted on a planned basis, so small issues are caught before they become expensive ones. It also keeps your compliance records current and, on our installations, supports the longer pro-rata guarantees." },
    { "q": "What equipment do you cover?", "a": "We service the full range of water treatment equipment, including water softeners, reverse osmosis plant, filters, pumps, valves and dosing systems. Because these components work together, we look at the system as a whole rather than treating each part in isolation. That way a change in one area is not left to cause a problem in another." },
    { "q": "What does it cost?", "a": "We do not sell fixed-price packages, because no two systems have the same equipment, demand or risk. Instead we tailor each service contract to your system and agree the scope and frequency with you, so you pay for the attention your installation actually needs. We are happy to visit, assess what is there, and set out a clear proposal before you commit." },
